# standing-grants.yml — CAPTAIN-SIGNED CEILING GRANTS [FI-2, sovereign kernel].
#
# A standing grant is the ONLY way a hard-ceiling row (external_comms,
# deploy_prod, spend, secrets, network_write, credentials_grant) resolves to
# an attributed allow in the sovereign posture — never unconditional auto, in
# ANY posture. Non-ceiling risk classes may NOT appear here (line-dropped).
#
# Fail-safe polarity (framework/authority/grants.py): absent / unparseable /
# not-schg-locked ⇒ grants resolve EMPTY (+ deduped need). Malformed rows are
# line-dropped.
#
# Class grantability is INSTANCE-scoped (Captain ruling 2026-07-05 — the old
# flavor=personal structural refusal is gone): a `never_grant:` list in the
# Captain-locked instance/config/posture.yml drops every grant row whose
# risk_class is listed, fail-closed at load, + ONE kind=decision need per
# class (never a recurring grant-request need). Empty/absent never_grant =
# all six ceiling classes grantable — the rows below still decide. E.g.
# Nate's personal instance keeps external outbound per-item-approved
# (ACT-AND-DRAFT) via, in posture.yml:
#   never_grant: [external_comms]
#
# Every row is enforced with ALL of: deployment==CABINET_ID, action_type +
# lane membership (named lanes only — never '*'), unexpired (expires ≤ 90d
# after granted_at), unrevoked (file flag OR Redis tombstone
# cabinet:grant:revoked:<id>; Redis unreachable ⇒ treated revoked), daily
# rate (cabinet:grant:count:<id>:<date>; unreadable ⇒ not granted), no active
# Captain veto, and the class HARD-SCOPE predicate:
#   external_comms → recipient ∈ scope.recipient_allowlist (glob ok)
#   spend          → amount_eur ≤ scope.max_eur_per_day
#   others         → vendor ∈ scope.vendor_allowlist
#
# Grants change ONLY via `sudo bash cabinet/scripts/grant-apply.sh NEED-<hex>`
# in an unlock window (D7) — there is no runtime writer. `basis` cites the
# NEED fingerprint that argued for the grant.
#
# Activate: cp → edit → commit → sudo chflags schg instance/config/standing-grants.yml
version: 1
grants:
  - {id: GRANT-example-stepnetwork-mail, deployment: mini-polads,
     risk_class: external_comms, action_types: [external_email],
     lanes: [polads],
     scope: {recipient_allowlist: ["*@stepnetwork.dk"], max_eur_per_day: 0,
             vendor_allowlist: []},
     rate: {max_per_day: 10}, expires: 2026-10-03,
     granted_by: "Captain (Nate)", granted_at: 2026-07-05T00:00:00Z,
     basis: "NEED-1a2b3c4d", revoked: false}
